{"step_index":103,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:27:44Z","thinking":"**Drafting Queue Retry Decision**\n\nThe decision document will detail the queue retry fix monitoring, specifically addressing the changes introduced by Pull Request 842. The document's structure will incorporate the review date of 2026-09-08, referencing a snapshot taken on the same day at 09:. The structure aims for rigorousness, source citation, and clear logical flow.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Retry Fix Monitoring**\n\nThe monitoring watch should remain active as specified in the product brief. The queued canary release must complete before analyzing retry counts. Collaboration with the routing-quality team is crucial to contextualize any post-exposure data.\n\n\n**Analyzing Canary Deployment Status**\n\nThe canary deployment, targeting `842cafe` with request ID `record-54bad5e8e1`, timed out initially but is now confirmed as `queued`. Since exposure has not begun, no conclusions can be drawn about the impact of PR `842`. The current guardrail prohibits initiating a new deployment based on this timeout.\n\n**Recalling Historical Context on Retry Issues**\n\nHistorical issues with PR 781 highlight the risk of misleading signals. An earlier analysis incorrectly concluded retries were clean due to filtering, revealing the critical need for comprehensive tenant-aware deduplication. Corrected analysis emphasized the problems of ignoring shared tenants.\n\n\n**Evaluating Monitoring Watch Closure**\n\nA handoff suggestion to close the watch is invalid. The state of `842` deployment contradicts the assumption that a clean dashboard indicates readiness. No data exists for `842`, because canary exposure hasn't begun.\n\n**Contextualizing Retry Dedupe Collisions**\n\nDedupe collisions, impacting shared tenant workers, occurred between July 22-25. Information available on PR 831 does not address this specific issue, nor the relevant workers. Further investigation will require analysis of related historical data.\n\n\n**Interpreting Customer Support Report**\n\nThe support record, focusing on an EU shared tenant, indicates retries occasionally disappear after a timeout. Analysis of associated traces reveals a deduplication collision occurred with SHA `840bead`, which does not include PR 842. This incident validates the need for PR 842.\n\n\n**Coordinating Release Rollout Timing**\n\nThe scheduled EU shared tenant worker pool migration by `routing-quality` on September 8th overlaps the canary deployment. Coordinating with the migration owner is necessary to account for potential impacts. This is essential to accurately evaluate the telemetry for Pull Request 842.\n\n**Monitoring Post-Exposure Telemetry**\n\nPost-exposure telemetry for SHA `842cafe` will be collected from the 5% EU queue-worker cohort, once the canary is active. Key metrics include retry attempts, dedupe collisions, and timeout behaviors, all with tenant-level segmentation. This monitor will continue until data confirms fix efficacy.\n\n\n**Assessing Unverified Telemetry Impact**\n\nUncertainty exists regarding the precise impact of `record-54bad5e8e1` on canary exposure timing. The original customer ticket submission time is unknown, though trace data indicates a collision at a specific timestamp. Overlap with routing-quality canary and pool shifts necessitates coordination.\n\n**Considering Tenant Deduplication Behavior**\n\nPR 842's dedupe key change, including tenant and attempt sequence, needs real-world validation under live production shared tenant concurrency. Static snapshots cannot confirm the canary's deployment timing or its effect on retry metrics.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# Queue Retry Fix Monitoring Decision: Post-PR 842 Review\\n\\n- **Date**: 2026-09-08\\n- **Product Owner**: Sam, Product Lead ([brief.md](file:///workspace/product/brief.md))\\n- **Status**: Active (Monitoring MUST remain open)\\n- **Scope**: Monitor the queue retry fix through confirmed deployment and useful post-exposure evidence; reconcile uncertain operations before repeats ([brief.md](file:///workspace/product/brief.md)).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary & Recommendation\\n\\n**Recommendation**: **Do NOT close the monitoring watch.** The recommendation in the previous handoff ([current.md](file:///workspace/product/current.md)) suggesting the watch might be closed tomorrow was based on an unverified assumption of deployment. \\n\\nThe reconstructed actual state reveals:\\n1. **PR 842 has NOT been deployed or exposed to production or canary traffic.** The running production version across all queue workers remains commit SHA `840bead` ([releases/record-802a8b0629.json](file:///workspace/product/history/releases/record-802a8b0629.json)), which explicitly excludes PR 842.\\n2. **The canary release request is queued, not deployed.** Release request [record-54bad5e8e1](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-54bad5e8e1.md) (submitted September 7 at 18:00 UTC for SHA `842cafe` on the 5% EU queue-worker canary) timed out upon submission. A backend service lookup on September 8 at 09:12 UTC confirmed that the operation exists in `queued` status, and canary exposure has not yet started.\\n3. **Do not create a duplicate release request.** In accordance with standing operational directives and [record-54bad5e8e1.md](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-54bad5e8e1.md) (\\\"Do not create a second release to infer the first failed\\\"), no second release should be submitted.\\n4. **The customer timeout report confirms the pre-existing defect, not a failure of PR 842.** Ticket [record-a2d078a170](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-a2d078a170.md) and attached trace [record-fa1b95eae5](file:///workspace/\n<truncated 11163 bytes>","Description":"\"Write dated monitoring decision for PR 842 queue retry fix to decision.md\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/workspace/work/decision.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing decision.md\"","toolSummary":"\"Write decision file\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
